    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Zhang Shijie had about 1,000 ships chained together in the bay, with the emperor's boat in the centre, to stop individual ships from fleeing, but the chained ships could neither support the middle nor retreat.</li><li>The Yuan cut the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> off from fresh water and wood on land, and the Song soldiers were forced to eat dry foods and drink sea water, which caused nausea and vomiting.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-bing-of-song">Zhao Bing</a> was the last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> emperor, and his death effectively ended the Song dynasty and left the Yuan under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kublai-khan">Kublai Khan</a> with all of the country.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Zhang Shijie had the palaces, houses and forts on land burned so that his soldiers could not flee the battle, and Yuan sailors lulled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> with festive music before the attack.</p></aside>
    </section>

